4.2 Configuration du worker : /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties

Une seule ligne change d’un worker à l’autre : rest.advertised.host.name.

cat > /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties <<'EOF'
############ Cluster Kafka ############
bootstrap.servers=mcq-dbk70.cgi.credit-cgi.fr:9092,mcq-dbk71.cgi.credit-cgi.fr:9092,mcq-dbk72.cgi.credit-cgi.fr:9092
security.protocol=SASL_PLAINTEXT
sasl.mechanism=SCRAM-SHA-512
sasl.jaas.config=org.apache.kafka.common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username="connect" password="<CONNECT_PW>";

# Les producteurs et consommateurs des tâches ne reprennent PAS la section ci-dessus : on la répète
producer.security.protocol=SASL_PLAINTEXT
producer.sasl.mechanism=SCRAM-SHA-512
producer.sasl.jaas.config=org.apache.kafka.common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username="connect" password="<CONNECT_PW>";
consumer.security.protocol=SASL_PLAINTEXT
consumer.sasl.mechanism=SCRAM-SHA-512
consumer.sasl.jaas.config=org.apache.kafka.common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username="connect" password="<CONNECT_PW>";
admin.security.protocol=SASL_PLAINTEXT
admin.sasl.mechanism=SCRAM-SHA-512
admin.sasl.jaas.config=org.apache.kafka.common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username="connect" password="<CONNECT_PW>";

############ Cluster Connect ############
group.id=connect-cdc
config.storage.topic=connect-cdc-configs
offset.storage.topic=connect-cdc-offsets
status.storage.topic=connect-cdc-status
config.storage.replication.factor=3
offset.storage.replication.factor=3
status.storage.replication.factor=3
offset.flush.interval.ms=10000

############ Format des messages (surchargeable par connecteur) ############
key.converter=org.apache.kafka.connect.json.JsonConverter
value.converter=org.apache.kafka.connect.json.JsonConverter
key.converter.schemas.enable=false
value.converter.schemas.enable=false

############ Création des topics de données par Debezium ############
topic.creation.enable=true

############ Plugins ############
plugin.path=/opt/kafka/plugins

############ API REST ############
listeners=http://0.0.0.0:8083
rest.advertised.host.name=mcq-dbz70.cgi.credit-cgi.fr
rest.advertised.port=8083
rest.extension.classes=org.apache.kafka.connect.rest.basic.auth.extension.BasicAuthSecurityRestExtension
EOF
HOST=mcq-dbz70; sed -i "s/^rest.advertised.host.name=.*/rest.advertised.host.name=$HOST.cgi.credit-cgi.fr/" /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties
read -rsp 'PW connect (SCRAM) : ' PW; echo; sed -i "s#<CONNECT_PW>#$PW#g" /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties; unset PW
chown root:kafka /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties && chmod 640 /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties && grep -c '<CONNECT_PW>' /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties

➡️ Le grep doit afficher 0.

4.3 Authentification Basic de l’API REST

Générez une fois deux mots de passe, identiques sur les 2 workers, et rangez-les dans votre coffre :

for u in connect-admin akhq-connect; do echo "$u : $(openssl rand -base64 24)"; done

Fichier JAAS :

cat > /etc/kafka/connect-rest-jaas.conf <<'EOF'
KafkaConnect {
  org.apache.kafka.connect.rest.basic.auth.extension.PropertyFileLoginModule required
  file="/etc/kafka/connect-rest-users.properties";
};
EOF

Fichier des comptes, au format utilisateur: motdepasse :

umask 027; read -rsp 'PW connect-admin : ' P1; echo; read -rsp 'PW akhq-connect : ' P2; echo; printf 'connect-admin: %s\nakhq-connect: %s\n' "$P1" "$P2" > /etc/kafka/connect-rest-users.properties; unset P1 P2

Droits sur les fichiers :

chown root:kafka /etc/kafka/connect-rest-*.{conf,properties} && chmod 640 /etc/kafka/connect-rest-users.properties && chmod 644 /etc/kafka/connect-rest-jaas.conf
cp /opt/kafka/current/config/connect-log4j.properties /etc/kafka/ && chmod 644 /etc/kafka/connect-log4j.properties
4.4 Unit systemd

La heap est à 8 Go si la machine a 16 Go de RAM. Avec moins, mettez la moitié de la RAM disponible.

cat > /etc/systemd/system/kafka-connect.service <<'EOF'
[Unit]
Description=Kafka Connect distributed worker (Debezium)
Wants=network-online.target
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=kafka
Group=kafka
Environment=JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/jre-21-openjdk
Environment="KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS=-Xms8g -Xmx8g"
Environment=LOG_DIR=/var/log/kafka
Environment="KAFKA_LOG4J_OPTS=-Dlog4j.configuration=file:/etc/kafka/connect-log4j.properties"
Environment="KAFKA_OPTS=-Djava.security.auth.login.config=/etc/kafka/connect-rest-jaas.conf"
ExecStart=/opt/kafka/current/bin/connect-distributed.sh /etc/kafka/connect-distributed.properties
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=15
TimeoutStopSec=120
SuccessExitStatus=143
LimitNOFILE=100000

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
EOF
systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl enable --now kafka-connect
4.5 Vérifications

Sur chaque worker (le démarrage prend 30 à 60 secondes) :

systemctl is-active kafka-connect; ss -ltn | grep -c ':8083'; ausearch -m avc -ts recent | grep -c denied
grep -E 'ERROR|Joined group|Finished starting connectors and tasks' /var/log/kafka/connect.log | tail -5

Depuis la toolbox, ou depuis n’importe quel poste du réseau :

Accès sans identifiants, qui doit être refusé :

curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://mcq-dbz70.cgi.credit-cgi.fr:8083/

Version :

read -rsp 'PW connect-admin : ' CA; echo; curl -s -u "connect-admin:$CA" http://mcq-dbz70.cgi.credit-cgi.fr:8083/

Plugins chargés :

curl -s -u "connect-admin:$CA" http://mcq-dbz71.cgi.credit-cgi.fr:8083/connector-plugins | grep -oE '"class":"[^"]+"'

Les 2 workers doivent faire partie du même groupe connect-cdc :

$K/kafka-consumer-groups.sh $ADM --describe --group connect-cdc --members 2>/dev/null | grep -c dbz
